codemap 9
tour behaviour-pin
kind layer
author ai
group tests
note How a change proves what it did to the tool's behaviour. The harness lives in crates/codemap/tests: common/ holds the fixture, the runners and every scenario; cli.rs and gui.rs turn the scenario lists into one #[test] each, parity.rs plays them against two builds, and features.rs checks the feature registry against the map. cargo test replays every CLI command against a generated fixture repo and plays scripted GUI scenarios in real windows, and ran fails a scenario that crashed or printed a script error; nothing compares output to a file. A refactor instead runs the parity test, which plays every scenario with the old build and the new one and compares transcripts, GUI dumps and screenshots byte for byte. Every run sees a PATH with jj and git and no language server, so every file is indexed by tree-sitter and the output is the same on every run; a scenario that needs jj or git skips itself, with the reason on stderr, when that tool is not installed.

