note Plays a GUI scenario and returns its stderr and the output of its after commands. A script line aiming at <<prefix>> is resolved first by a probe run of the script up to that line, on a fresh fixture, which ends with a dump of the frame that line runs in, reading the rectangle from that dump (or an earlier rect line); the final run then starts from the same state. <<prefix>> stands for the centre of the last stderr line starting with prefix, <<prefix|dx,dy>> for a point offset from its top-left corner. Offsets are pixels: the scripts assume the fixed 1600x1000 script window at scale 1, 16 px rows. A script: line in the final run's stderr is left in the returned text; ran fails the scenario on it, so a missed gesture cannot pass. The screenshots land in shots(name).

